          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Understanding acids and bases is essential in chemistry. A Brønsted-Lowry acid donates a proton, while a Brønsted-Lowry base accepts a proton. This proton transfer forms conjugate acids and bases. Water is an important substance in this context, as it can act as both an acid and a base, maintaining a balance of hydronium and hydroxide ions."
              }
            ],
            "id": "1489968309",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The acidity or basicity of a solution is measured using pH and pOH. These concepts help explain everyday phenomena, from the acidity of rainwater to the pH balance in our bodies, highlighting the importance of acids and bases in both scientific and daily contexts."
              }
            ],
            "id": "2n8md5dwkln8dkz",
            "type": "p"
          }
